NetBeans Edit Externally changelog
==================================


Version 2.0.0 - 2026-08-03
--------------------------

	- [BREAKING] Explicitly specify position of menu items
		- This leads to a different menu item ordering
	- [BREAKING] Explicitly set the parent folder of the edited file as working
		directory.
		- This should not have any influence on most users may lead to a
			different behaviour in the editor (different relative file paths,
			location of temporary files, etc.)
	- Provide new placeholders for the selected text.
		- Such placeholders already were implemented, but intentionally not
			documented. They are now refined and ready for public use.
	- Do not activate plugin if no file is selected
	- Fix parsing bug of literal dollar sign
	- Fix possible lockup if called external command produces a lot of output
		on stdout/stderr
	- Refer for online help to the GitHub README
		- The old approach via JavaHelp wasn't working in Apache NetBeans
		anymore anyway
	- Emit warning message for unknown placeholders (may be a typo)
	- Do not clutter the logfile with info messages when validating
		commandlines
	- The GitHub repository now provides a wike page for documenting
		commandlines to be used with this plugin.


Version 1.0.4 - 2026-07-02
--------------------------

	- Fix bug in parsing commandline message
	- Drop support for Java < 17


Version 1.0.3 - 2024-04-04
--------------------------

	- Correct wording of two messages


Version 1.0.2 - 2024-04-02
--------------------------

	- Changed Apache NetBeans Plugin Portal


Version 1.0.1 - 2019-08-15
--------------------------

	- Fix escaping of paths under MS Windows(#1)


Version 1.0.0 - 2019-08-12
--------------------------

	- Initial release
